WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.700
In mice, one cluster of MRG -PR genes can be deleted.

2
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.420
Those mice scratch normally to histamine.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.020
They scratch much less to chloroquine.

4
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.360
If itch were only a histamine response, that could not happen.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.100
So is itch a sense of its own, or only weak pain?

6
00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.453
Next, researchers removed one group of neurons from mice.

7
00:00:25.073 --> 00:00:28.833
These neurons are marked by MrgprA3.

8
00:00:29.373 --> 00:00:31.373
Scratching fell, histamine included.

9
00:00:31.993 --> 00:00:34.753
The pain assays they tested did not change.

10
00:00:35.313 --> 00:00:39.393
In the cheek assay, an itch substance evokes scratching with a hindpaw.

11
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:42.653
A pain substance evokes wiping with a forelimb.

12
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:45.517
A second experiment put one thing back.

13
00:00:46.097 --> 00:00:47.977
Capsaicin normally evokes wiping.

14
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:56.597
The researchers restored working TRPV1 only in the MrgprA3 neurons, in mice that

15
00:00:56.597 --> 00:00:57.697
otherwise lacked it.

16
00:00:58.277 --> 00:01:00.757
Capsaicin then evoked itch -related behavior.

17
00:01:01.477 --> 00:01:04.397
Ablation shows these neurons are needed in these assays.

18
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:08.037
The rescue shows what they can drive when they alone respond.

19
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:12.410
One mouse relay starts with Nppb from sensory neurons.

20
00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:17.690
Mice without Nppb lost almost all responses to the tested itch agents.

21
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:23.150
Nppb injected around the cord still evoked scratching in those mice and in normal

22
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:30.590
mice. About 70 % of the cells with the Nppb receptor, N -P -R -A, were removed.

23
00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.210
G -R -P still evoked scratching.

24
00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:41.370
One route fits: sensory Nppb, then N -P -R -A cells, then G -R -P and G -R -P -R.

25
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.650
Direct contacts were not shown.

26
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.470
The contested step is where the GRP comes from.

27
00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:53.590
In one study, deleting GRP in sensory neurons reduced scratching that does not use

28
00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:59.230
histamine. Removing spinal GRP neurons did not reduce itch in that study's tests.

29
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.650
Another study reported the opposite for spinal neurons.

30
00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.190
These results do not settle on one source.

31
00:02:05.983 --> 00:02:12.983
Keep the scope. A later mouse study used fast ionotropic stimulation of MRG -PRA3

32
00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:15.843
neurons. It mostly evoked pain type behavior.

33
00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:19.423
GQ -linked stimulation evoked itch behaviour.

34
00:02:20.143 --> 00:02:23.643
So these neurons are not itch only under every manipulation.

35
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:29.103
Nothing here shows that people carry a MRG -PRA3 lineage.

36
00:02:29.703 --> 00:02:32.823
Being needed in an assay does not make a line itch only.
